      ":question/problem": "$\\int (1\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+3\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}\u2061x\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+3\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =1\\int \\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\operatorname{csc}\u2061x\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x+3(-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x)+C \\\\  & =1\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x-3\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
